# Astra AI — full user data by default

Applies to **astra-frontend**, **astra-backend**, and **MyProjectName** (mobile) whenever you build or change AI features: insights panels, assistant chat context, quotes, coaching, analytics AI, or any future Groq/LLM surface.

## Default rule (mandatory)

**Always give the AI the signed-in user’s data from all Life OS modules**, unless the human prompt **explicitly** says to omit a field, module, or category.

Modules to include by default (non-exhaustive — include new modules the same way):

- Profile / settings (currency, timezone, AI prefs, etc.)
- Tasks & projects
- Time track
- Goals
- Wealth (respect currency formatting)
- Health (weight, BMI, ideal weight, height, water, sleep, exercise, workouts, mood, habits linked to health)
- Habits
- Notes
- Analytics / life score / dashboard aggregates

## Opt-out only

Do **not** omit data because:

- “This page is only about X”
- “Keep the payload small”
- “Insights are water/sleep focused”
- Convenience or partial snapshots

**Only** skip something when the user prompt clearly says e.g. “do not send wealth”, “exclude notes”, “omit weight”.

## Implementation checklist

When adding or editing an AI insight / chat context builder:

1. Start from **all available user/module fields** for that request (or a shared full-context builder).
2. If building a page-scoped insight, still include **cross-module** facts the model needs (e.g. Health insights must include weight/BMI/ideal weight, not only water/sleep).
3. Prefer one shared context assembler over per-page hand-picked subsets.
4. Cache keys must include a context fingerprint so new fields regenerate AI output.
5. Never invent numbers — only send real data; if a module has no data yet, send null/empty, don’t drop the key silently without reason.

## Examples

```ts
// ❌ BAD — page-local subset; weight never reaches the model
const insightContext = {
  waterGlasses, sleepHours, exerciseMinutes, habitsProgress,
}

// ✅ GOOD — include all health (and relevant cross-module) user data
const insightContext = {
  waterGlasses, sleepHours, exerciseMinutes, habitsProgress,
  latestWeightKg, heightCm, idealWeightKg, bmi, bmiLabel,
  healthyWeightDelta, idealWeightDelta, recentWeights, moodToday,
  // …other modules the user has data for, unless prompt says omit
}
```

## Secrets

Still never send passwords, OTPs, reset tokens, raw refresh tokens, or other secrets. Full **product data** ≠ secrets.

